<!--
  Chapter 31 — Data Consistency.
    reads/     read-your-writes and monotonic reads over a primary and an asynchronous replica: consistency
               tokens (WAL positions), wait-briefly-then-primary routing
    profiles/  profile updates with If-Match versions (no lost updates through the API) and token-routed reads
    points/    loyalty points without lost updates: atomic and conditional updates
    merge/     convergent merges for data written in two places: OR-Set, hybrid logical clock, LWW register
    verify/    the chapter's experiments on a PostgreSQL primary with two streaming replicas
-->
